{"availability":"available","full":"damiansire/web-worker-patterns","name":"web-worker-patterns","description":"An interactive platform demonstrating advanced Web Worker patterns and architectural strategies.","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":173,"forks":9,"created":"2025-10-18T13:29:56Z","updated":"2026-10-06T06:31:02Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://damiansire.github.io/web-worker-patterns/","topics":["angular","concurrency","education","javascript","multithreading","patterns","performance","typescript","web-workers"],"demo":"https://damiansire.github.io/web-worker-patterns/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:04.375Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:04.375Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T02:54:04.375Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:04.375Z","stars":173,"forks":9}],"technologies":["Angular"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Note on example 12 (SharedArrayBuffer). It needs cross-origin isolation (COOP/COEP), and GitHub Pages can't send custom response headers. The app ships a service-worker shim (public/coi-serviceworker.js) that re-adds those headers client-side so crossOriginIsolated becomes true on the deployed demo. If isolation still isn't available, the example detects it at runtime and falls back to a clearly labelled simulated backend instead of failing silently. See example 12 for detail.","Interactive educational platform about Web Workers built with Angular 22. It ships 16 progressive examples with live demos and real thread visualization. The UI is in Spanish, and the presentation is a swappable theme layer: today a light theme (default), its dark counterpart (midnight) and a playable one (rpg), switchable live, with the engine kept generic so more themes (and languages) can be added without touching the domain.","▶ Live demo: damiansire.github.io/web-worker-patterns"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/damiansire/web-worker-patterns/blob/